<title>INDIA: Indian Aug infrastructure output up 2.2 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Indian Aug infrastructure output up 2.2 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian industrial production in six leading infrastructure sectors increased by 2.2 percent in August over the same month in 1995, a government statement said on Wednesday.  </p>
<p>The new monthly breakdown of industrial production covered electricity, coal, saleable steel, crude oil, cement and petroleum products.</p>
<p>These industries account for 28.8 percent of the monthly index of industrial production, the statement said.  </p>
<p>    INDUSTRIAL PRODUCTION     Aug 96    Apr-Aug 96   Apr-Aug 95</p>
<p>Year-on-year change</p>
<p>     -Electricity		 +2.2	 +2.4	    +11.7</p>
<p>     -Coal			  +2.2	 +8.9	     +9.6</p>
<p>     -Saleable steel	    +2.1	 +4.6	    +11.8</p>
<p>     -Crude oil		  -11.8	-10.4	    +19.0</p>
<p>     -Refinery Products	+15.6	 +7.3	     +4.8</p>
<p>     -Cement		     +14.9	+13.8	    +11.3</p>
</text>
